{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "metadata": {
  "note": "North County Transit District rail in San Diego County. The COASTER commuter train opened on 27 February 1995 between Oceanside and downtown San Diego over the old Santa Fe Surf Line, and the SPRINTER, a diesel light rail line running inland from Oceanside to Escondido, followed on 9 March 2008 over a freight branch that had not carried passengers in decades. Both carry one NCTD colour under Rule 4.",
  "sources": [
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coaster_(rail_service) (1995 opening, Oceanside–San Diego over the former Santa Fe Surf Line, 41 mi)",
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprinter_(rail_service) (2008 opening, Oceanside–Escondido, 22 mi)",
   "OpenStreetMap route relations, extracted 29 August 2026; traced length is compared with the documented route length on each feature."
  ],
  "not_yet_sourced": "Headways and speeds are estimates; no NCTD timetable was consulted. The COASTER relation is tagged operator TransitAmerica, the contract operator, rather than NCTD, which owns the service — NCTD is used as the company here."
 },
